questions.statement:
Consider the following pseudo-code algorithm segment:

```
algo-1() {
  for all vertices u {
    num(u) = 0
  }
  edges = null
  i = 1
  while there is a vertex v such that num(v) == 0 {
    num(v) = i++
    enqueue(v)
    while queue is not empty {
      v = dequeue()
      for all vertices u adjacent to v {
        if num(u) == 0 {
          num(u) = i++
          enqueue(u)
          attach edge (uv) to edges
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

What does the above algorithm describe?

What does the following piece of code do?

```c
void Insert(struct Node *Start)
{
    struct node *ptr, *temp;
    ptr = CreateNode(); // CreateNode() creates a node.
    if (Start == NULL)
        Start = ptr;
    else
    {
        temp = Start;
        Start = ptr;
        ptr->link = temp;
    }
}
```
